1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,840
In the last five HSC Chemistry papers, calculate

2
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:05,920
was the second most common command in the

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,440
written section, after explain, and the commonest value

4
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:10,640
was four marks.

5
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:13,440
In every one of the last six Chemistry

6
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:17,040
marking feedback reports, NESA flagged the same kinds

7
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:20,640
of problem: hidden steps, lost units, or rounding

8
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:21,640
too early.

9
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,200
Recent Biology papers didn't use the word calculate,

10
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:28,000
but still asked for numbers, like a probability

11
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:30,080
or a number of people from a graph.

12
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:32,880
So let's set out a calculation a marker

13
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:33,760
can follow.

14
00:00:34,967 --> 00:00:37,526
Here's an HSC-style Chemistry question.

15
00:00:38,167 --> 00:00:41,206
Sixty millilitres of hydrochloric acid is mixed with

16
00:00:41,367 --> 00:00:44,486
forty millilitres of sodium hydroxide solution in a

17
00:00:44,567 --> 00:00:47,686
polystyrene cup, and the temperature rises from twenty

18
00:00:47,847 --> 00:00:51,206
point six to twenty five point eight degrees.

19
00:00:51,287 --> 00:00:53,446
The question asks you to calculate the molar

20
00:00:53,607 --> 00:00:55,686
enthalpy of neutralisation.

21
00:00:55,767 --> 00:00:56,806
Four marks.

22
00:00:56,887 --> 00:00:58,886
If you take Biology, you don't need the

23
00:00:59,127 --> 00:01:00,166
chemistry here.

24
00:01:00,287 --> 00:01:02,566
Watch how each line is laid out: your

25
00:01:02,767 --> 00:01:03,686
question is coming.

26
00:01:04,901 --> 00:01:06,020
Run the routine.

27
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:09,300
The verb is calculate: work out an answer

28
00:01:09,380 --> 00:01:10,740
from the information given.

29
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:13,860
Four marks for one number is a hint:

30
00:01:13,940 --> 00:01:15,340
there are steps to show.

31
00:01:15,540 --> 00:01:18,340
The thing asked for is a molar enthalpy,

32
00:01:18,420 --> 00:01:21,300
so the answer needs kilojoules per mole, and

33
00:01:21,460 --> 00:01:22,100
a sign.

34
00:01:22,660 --> 00:01:23,540
Now the givens.

35
00:01:23,940 --> 00:01:25,460
Don't copy them into a list.

36
00:01:25,700 --> 00:01:28,180
You'll underline each one as you use it.

37
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:32,280
Every calculation answer can follow the same four

38
00:01:32,440 --> 00:01:33,200
steps.

39
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:34,520
Write the equation.

40
00:01:34,920 --> 00:01:37,240
Substitute the values, with their units.

41
00:01:37,720 --> 00:01:40,280
Solve, and give the answer with units and

42
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:42,040
sensible significant figures.

43
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:44,920
Then sense check: are the size and the

44
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,120
sign believable?

45
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:49,320
Here's the memory aid: one E and three

46
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:50,160
S's.

47
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:53,800
Equation, substitute, solve, sense check.

48
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,760
Step one, the heat: q equals m c

49
00:01:58,920 --> 00:01:59,920
delta T.

50
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:03,000
The mass is both solutions together, a hundred

51
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:05,400
millilitres, so one hundred grams.

52
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:08,440
Delta T is twenty five point eight minus

53
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:11,520
twenty point six: five point two degrees.

54
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:15,560
Substitute, with units: one hundred, times four point

55
00:02:15,640 --> 00:02:18,040
one eight, times five point two.

56
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:20,360
That's two thousand, one hundred and seventy three

57
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:23,800
point six joules, or two point one seven

58
00:02:23,880 --> 00:02:25,640
three six kilojoules.

59
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:27,000
Keep every digit.

60
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:30,680
Step two, the moles of water.

61
00:02:31,160 --> 00:02:34,920
Acid: zero point zero six zero zero litres,

62
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:38,280
times zero point eight zero zero, gives zero

63
00:02:38,440 --> 00:02:40,960
point zero four eight zero moles.

64
00:02:41,240 --> 00:02:44,920
Base: zero point zero four zero zero litres,

65
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:48,280
times one point zero zero, gives zero point

66
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:50,440
zero four zero zero moles.

67
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:53,160
The base runs out first, so it sets

68
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:55,960
the water: zero point zero four zero zero

69
00:02:56,120 --> 00:02:56,680
moles.

70
00:02:57,160 --> 00:02:58,360
Write that sentence.

71
00:02:58,520 --> 00:03:00,920
It tells the marker which value you chose,

72
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:01,720
and why.

73
00:03:02,934 --> 00:03:06,373
Step three: divide, then add the sign.

74
00:03:06,614 --> 00:03:09,573
Two point one seven three six kilojoules over

75
00:03:09,694 --> 00:03:12,773
zero point zero four zero zero moles is

76
00:03:12,814 --> 00:03:14,933
fifty four point three four.

77
00:03:14,974 --> 00:03:17,733
The temperature rose, so heat was released, and

78
00:03:17,814 --> 00:03:19,413
delta H is negative.

79
00:03:19,814 --> 00:03:22,693
Round once, at the end: minus fifty four

80
00:03:22,854 --> 00:03:24,053
kilojoules per mole.

81
00:03:24,614 --> 00:03:25,773
Now the sense check.

82
00:03:25,974 --> 00:03:29,173
The usual value is about minus fifty seven.

83
00:03:29,214 --> 00:03:31,493
Ours is a little less negative, which fits

84
00:03:31,574 --> 00:03:32,933
some heat loss from the cup.

85
00:03:34,134 --> 00:03:36,693
Why fifty four, and not fifty four point

86
00:03:36,894 --> 00:03:37,573
three?

87
00:03:37,654 --> 00:03:39,893
An answer is only as precise as its

88
00:03:39,974 --> 00:03:41,653
least precise measurement.

89
00:03:41,974 --> 00:03:44,813
Most values here have three significant figures.

90
00:03:45,094 --> 00:03:47,493
But delta T came from a subtraction, which

91
00:03:47,574 --> 00:03:51,173
keeps decimal places, not figures: five point two

92
00:03:51,414 --> 00:03:52,493
has only two.

93
00:03:52,774 --> 00:03:55,093
Exact numbers, like a count or a mole

94
00:03:55,174 --> 00:03:57,053
ratio, never limit you.

95
00:03:57,334 --> 00:04:00,373
Several recent marking guidelines named significant figures in

96
00:04:00,454 --> 00:04:03,413
the top band, and in one three-mark question,

97
00:04:03,614 --> 00:04:06,213
correct working with the wrong significant figures got

98
00:04:06,294 --> 00:04:06,693
two.

99
00:04:07,334 --> 00:04:09,813
Not every guideline mentions them, so get them

100
00:04:09,934 --> 00:04:11,173
right every time.

101
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:13,720
And round only once.

102
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:16,240
If you'd rounded the heat to two point

103
00:04:16,320 --> 00:04:19,200
two kilojoules halfway through, you'd get minus fifty

104
00:04:19,360 --> 00:04:22,080
five, not minus fifty four.

105
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:24,880
NESA's own sample answers keep the extra digits

106
00:04:24,960 --> 00:04:26,920
until the last line.

107
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:30,160
Sometimes a range is accepted: when values are

108
00:04:30,240 --> 00:04:32,760
read off a graph, one guideline left the

109
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:35,600
acceptable range of readings to the marking centre.

110
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:38,240
That allows for reading, not for rounding.

111
00:04:39,467 --> 00:04:41,386
Now suppose you slip.

112
00:04:41,467 --> 00:04:44,026
Two students divide by the acid's moles, and

113
00:04:44,107 --> 00:04:46,266
both get minus forty five.

114
00:04:46,427 --> 00:04:48,506
Answer A writes just that.

115
00:04:48,587 --> 00:04:50,986
Answer B shows every step.

116
00:04:51,027 --> 00:04:53,946
In our marking guide, A earns nothing.

117
00:04:54,027 --> 00:04:56,186
B is still wrong, but its right steps

118
00:04:56,267 --> 00:04:58,986
are visible, so B earns two for them.

119
00:04:59,067 --> 00:05:02,426
In one recent four-mark calculation, NESA's bands paid

120
00:05:02,507 --> 00:05:04,586
for the main steps, and for some relevant

121
00:05:04,667 --> 00:05:05,546
steps.

122
00:05:05,627 --> 00:05:08,106
But bands are set question by question, so

123
00:05:08,187 --> 00:05:10,426
don't count on carried-forward marks.

124
00:05:10,587 --> 00:05:12,586
Make every step visible.

125
00:05:12,627 --> 00:05:15,306
And a sense check helps: minus forty five

126
00:05:15,387 --> 00:05:18,266
is far from minus fifty seven, so recheck

127
00:05:18,347 --> 00:05:19,866
which reactant ran out.

128
00:05:21,067 --> 00:05:21,946
Your turn.

129
00:05:22,187 --> 00:05:24,506
Do the one in your subject, or both.

130
00:05:24,747 --> 00:05:25,706
Chemistry first.

131
00:05:26,347 --> 00:05:29,146
Zero point two zero zero grams of sodium

132
00:05:29,227 --> 00:05:32,026
hydroxide is dissolved and made up to two

133
00:05:32,107 --> 00:05:35,066
hundred and fifty point zero millilitres at twenty

134
00:05:35,147 --> 00:05:36,026
five degrees.

135
00:05:36,587 --> 00:05:38,866
Calculate the pH of the solution.

136
00:05:39,147 --> 00:05:40,066
Three marks.

137
00:05:40,267 --> 00:05:41,546
Pause here to answer.

138
00:05:51,967 --> 00:05:55,546
Moles: zero point two zero zero over forty

139
00:05:55,607 --> 00:05:59,006
point zero zero, five point zero zero times

140
00:05:59,087 --> 00:06:00,334
ten to the minus three.

141
00:06:00,399 --> 00:06:03,438
Divide by the litres: zero point zero two

142
00:06:03,503 --> 00:06:05,726
zero zero moles per litre.

143
00:06:05,807 --> 00:06:08,659
pOH is one point six nine nine, so

144
00:06:08,767 --> 00:06:12,286
pH is twelve point three zero one.

145
00:06:12,487 --> 00:06:16,206
Three significant figures in the hydroxide give three

146
00:06:16,287 --> 00:06:17,246
decimal places.

147
00:06:17,647 --> 00:06:19,726
It's a base, so above seven.

148
00:06:20,207 --> 00:06:22,526
The habit to drop: rounding to twelve point

149
00:06:22,687 --> 00:06:23,086
three.

150
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:25,660
Now Biology.

151
00:06:25,980 --> 00:06:28,700
Two hundred and fifty bearded dragons were genotyped

152
00:06:28,820 --> 00:06:31,820
at one snip, with alleles C and T.

153
00:06:32,540 --> 00:06:35,100
Ninety were C C, a hundred and ten

154
00:06:35,180 --> 00:06:38,140
were C T, and fifty were T T.

155
00:06:38,780 --> 00:06:41,180
Calculate the frequency of the T allele in

156
00:06:41,260 --> 00:06:41,980
this sample.

157
00:06:42,460 --> 00:06:43,180
Two marks.

158
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:44,860
Pause here to answer.

159
00:06:55,267 --> 00:06:59,266
Count alleles, not dragons: five hundred copies.

160
00:06:59,587 --> 00:07:01,906
T alleles: a hundred and ten from C

161
00:07:02,067 --> 00:07:04,626
T, plus a hundred from T T, makes

162
00:07:04,787 --> 00:07:06,146
two hundred and ten.

163
00:07:06,227 --> 00:07:09,106
Over five hundred, that's zero point four two.

164
00:07:09,667 --> 00:07:12,626
Counts are exact, and this divides exactly, so

165
00:07:12,867 --> 00:07:13,666
nothing to round.

166
00:07:14,227 --> 00:07:17,106
Check: C is zero point five eight, and

167
00:07:17,187 --> 00:07:18,626
together they make one.

168
00:07:19,347 --> 00:07:22,146
The habit to drop: fifty over two hundred

169
00:07:22,227 --> 00:07:24,226
and fifty, which counts dragons.

170
00:07:25,434 --> 00:07:28,153
So, every time you see calculate.

171
00:07:28,394 --> 00:07:29,433
Write the equation.

172
00:07:29,834 --> 00:07:32,473
Substitute with units, and say which value you

173
00:07:32,554 --> 00:07:33,953
chose and why.

174
00:07:34,234 --> 00:07:37,593
Solve, carrying every digit, then round once, to

175
00:07:37,674 --> 00:07:40,313
the least precise measurement, with the unit and

176
00:07:40,394 --> 00:07:41,353
the sign.

177
00:07:41,474 --> 00:07:44,313
Then sense check the size and the sign.

178
00:07:44,874 --> 00:07:46,313
Next: graphs and data

179
00:07:46,874 --> 00:07:47,113
questions.

180
00:07:48,334 --> 00:07:49,773
Here are the key notes.

181
00:07:50,014 --> 00:07:51,933
Pause the video if you need more time

182
00:07:52,014 --> 00:07:52,813
to copy them.
